WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.840
Imperial Grand Admiral, Chiss warrior,&nbsp;
bluest man in the galaxy — Thrawn is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.880
known as many things. Here's the&nbsp;
question, though: who is he really?

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.600
Although Thrawn was the main antagonist of&nbsp;
Star Wars Rebels for two of its four seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.040
precious little was revealed in the show&nbsp;
about his origins. However, the Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.280
Thrawn novels plug the gap nicely, revealing&nbsp;
much about Thrawn's people, the Chiss.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.040
The Chiss are a race living in the Unknown&nbsp;
Regions, an area made remote by cosmic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:35.040
obstacles such as black holes, keeping them&nbsp;
largely hidden from outsiders. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.720
this isolation acts as a double-edged sword, as&nbsp;
the people of the Unknown Regions lack access&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.400
to technologies that might have allowed them to&nbsp;
traverse the dangers of their region of space.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:50.240
Fortunately for the Chiss, some of their young&nbsp;
hold a strong connection to the Force, giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:55.600
them the ability to chart safe courses through&nbsp;
the Unknown Regions. However, the Chiss rarely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.880
if ever, venture out of their home area. This is&nbsp;
because they are governed by the ruling body known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:06.360
as the Chiss Ascendancy, which enacts policies&nbsp;
of secrecy to prevent the species' discovery.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:12.080
Though Thrawn's birth name was Kivu'raw'nuru, his&nbsp;
name is changed to "Mitth'raw'nuruodo" as a sign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.680
of respect during his successful military&nbsp;
career. The name ‘Thrawn’ comes from this;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.200
a short-hand name that combines his&nbsp;
new family name with his given name.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.920
The Chiss were not alone in the Unknown Regions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:27.720
however. Their biggest threat is&nbsp;
an alien race called the Grysk.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:32.040
Known for their warlike nature and mind&nbsp;
control abilities, the Grysk are ruled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:37.200
by a Hegemony very similar to the Galactic&nbsp;
Empire in makeup, with the biggest similarity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.920
between the two governments being a desire&nbsp;
to expand their influence at any cost. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:47.000
studying the Grysk and their tactics, Thrawn&nbsp;
inadvertently made himself an invaluable asset&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.560
for Palpatine's Empire. But the battle against&nbsp;
the Grysk wasn't without its own complications.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.440
While the Empire ruled the galaxy for&nbsp;
a relatively brief period of time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:00.560
the Grysk were established early enough that&nbsp;
they were able to monitor the Clone Wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.200
indicating their ambitions had been planned out&nbsp;
for some time. But while the Grysk certainly had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.240
designs to expand their empire, they had to&nbsp;
go through the Chiss to realize their goals.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.920
The Chiss Ascendancy realized this and sought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.320
allies to fight the Grysk — a task&nbsp;
eventually given to Captain Thrawn.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.480
Thrawn's loyalty to the Chiss stands&nbsp;
above all else. So how and why did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:26.080
he come to serve the Empire? The "why" is&nbsp;
surprisingly simple: the Chiss Ascendancy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.040
needed to determine whether the Empire&nbsp;
could help them defeat the Grysk Hegemony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.440
so they ordered Thrawn to join the Imperial&nbsp;
military. They wanted him to either convince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:39.040
the Empire to stand with the Chiss against&nbsp;
the Grysk, or manipulate events such that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.240
the Grysk would attack the Empire first,&nbsp;
giving the Chiss more time to prepare.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.640
The "how" is a bit more complicated. To help&nbsp;
convince the Empire he has nowhere else to go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.040
Thrawn fakes his exile from the Chiss.&nbsp;
Then he chooses a world he knows the Empire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.160
will eventually explore — and waits.&nbsp;
Once the Empire comes to the planet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.440
he slowly and methodically&nbsp;
picks off their scouting party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:05.320
eventually forcing their retreat. Thrawn takes&nbsp;
this opportunity to sneak aboard an Imperial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:09.560
ship and allow himself to be captured.&nbsp;
Once on board, he tells his "story" to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:14.801
the ranking officers. Impressed with his tactical&nbsp;
skills, they bring him before Emperor Palpatine.

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:17.545
[evil laughter]

00:03:17.545 --> 00:03:22.080
Thrawn gains favor with the Emperor on the&nbsp;
basis of his history with Anakin Skywalker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.360
whom he had met during the Clone Wars.&nbsp;
Although Thrawn doesn't receive any guarantees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.440
Palpatine does agree to consider helping the&nbsp;
Chiss if Thrawn serves the Empire faithfully.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.640
Although Thrawn ultimately swears allegiance&nbsp;
to the Empire and Palpatine, the effort he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:41.600
makes to gain the Emperor's trust proves that&nbsp;
his loyalty to the Chiss remained undimmed.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.400
While Thrawn holds up his end of the deal to serve&nbsp;
the Empire faithfully, his methods put him at odds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.840
with some high-ranking Imperial officials. In&nbsp;
order to protect himself from the threat of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:56.320
court-martial, he attends several parties held by&nbsp;
powerful members of the Empire. At one such party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:01.640
Thrawn comes into contact with Arihnda Pryce, an&nbsp;
ambitious government employee. Although nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:06.560
significant occurred in their first meeting, their&nbsp;
connection would prove to be mutually beneficial.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:11.800
When Pryce is blackmailed by a rival, Thrawn&nbsp;
gives her valuable advice to turn the tables. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:16.920
advice allows her to thwart her blackmailer&nbsp;
and become governor of the Lothal Sector.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:21.720
Some time later, Pryce and Thrawn work together&nbsp;
on a military campaign to crush a small group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:26.560
of rebels on the planet Batonn. Pryce is&nbsp;
responsible for a large number of civilian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:31.600
casualties during the uprising, which outrages&nbsp;
Thrawn. He initially plans on reporting Pryce's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.240
misdeeds to the Imperial Security Bureau, but&nbsp;
is convinced otherwise when Pryce offers to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:40.760
get Thrawn promoted to Grand Admiral —&nbsp;
a ranking Thrawn understandably covets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.960
as it would allow him to better proceed with&nbsp;
his primary mission for the Chiss. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.400
Pryce's offer comes with a catch: she will&nbsp;
only secure his promotion if Thrawn brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:55.280
his fleet to the Lothal system to deal with&nbsp;
the rebel cell known as Phoenix Squadron.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.600
Thrawn begins his war against Phoenix&nbsp;
Squadron almost immediately after receiving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.600
his promotion to Grand Admiral. Although&nbsp;
he finds an opportunity to destroy the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:08.840
rebel ship Ghost during a raid at Recklam&nbsp;
station, Thrawn allows the ship to go free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:14.080
in order to reel in a much larger prize: the&nbsp;
location of Phoenix Squadron's hidden base.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:18.440
In order to better understand how the rebels&nbsp;
operated, Thrawn spends much of his time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:23.520
analyzing their past and their strategies.&nbsp;
Thrawn's almost religious study of all things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:28.160
Phoenix Squadron pays big dividends when he&nbsp;
recognizes some distinctive artwork on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:33.720
helmet of a supposed "bounty hunter" captured&nbsp;
by Imperial Agent Kallus. After deducing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:39.360
bounty hunter is in fact Ezra Bridger, Thrawn&nbsp;
realizes Kallus was a double agent. He allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:44.160
him to continue operating as one until he&nbsp;
makes his next transmission. Thrawn then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:48.800
tracks the transmission to the planet of&nbsp;
Atollon and launches an all-out assault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.240
defeating and scattering the rebels. His&nbsp;
efforts to capture them are thwarted, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:59.480
by a creature known as the Bendu. After being shot&nbsp;
down, Thrawn's defeat is foretold by the Bendu.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:05.120
"I see your defeat, like many arms&nbsp;
surrounding you in a cold embrace."

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:08.520
Although Thrawn is victorious over&nbsp;
Phoenix Squadron in the short term,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:12.280
the Bendu's words eventually&nbsp;
come back to haunt him.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:14.040
After defeating the rebels on Atollon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:18.480
Thrawn is ordered by Palpatine to accompany&nbsp;
Darth Vader to investigate a disturbance in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:23.840
the force on Batuu — the same planet on which&nbsp;
Thrawn and Skywalker had first met. The two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:29.000
locate and capture a band of mysterious&nbsp;
aliens, who turn out to be Grysk agents.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.560
Thrawn and Vader lead an assault on the&nbsp;
Grysk base, and, after securing victory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:38.480
locate the source of the disturbance Palpatine&nbsp;
had felt: Force-sensitive Chiss children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:43.320
whom the Grysk had captured in order to make&nbsp;
them serve as navigators. Although Vader wants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:47.920
the children eliminated, Thrawn assures him that&nbsp;
the Force-sensitive Chiss would pose no threat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.400
since their connection to the Force&nbsp;
grows weaker when they reach adulthood.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:55.800
After rooting out the remaining Grysk and&nbsp;
rescuing more Chiss children, Thrawn returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:00.960
them to the Ascendancy; however, he also learns&nbsp;
that the Chiss are heading toward a civil war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:05.920
with the Grysk backing one of the Chiss factions.&nbsp;
Thrawn then reasons that, since the Grysk were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:10.560
attempting to capture navigators, it was likely&nbsp;
that they were preparing to eliminate the Chiss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.720
so they could wage war on the Empire. While Thrawn&nbsp;
continues to serve the Empire in the aftermath of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:21.360
this incident, these latest discoveries only&nbsp;
harden Thrawn's dedication to the Chiss cause.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:26.120
In order to curry favor with Palpatine and&nbsp;
convince him to help the Chiss against the Grysk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:30.920
Thrawn decides to develop a weapon that could&nbsp;
ensure the Empire's stability for years to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:35.320
come. He chooses to improve the standard&nbsp;
TIE fighter by giving it more firepower,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.840
a hyperdrive, and a deflector shield.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:42.920
The Rebel Alliance sees this new TIE fighter,&nbsp;
dubbed the TIE Defender, as a grave threat, since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:48.160
none of their X-wing craft have the firepower to&nbsp;
deal with its enhanced capabilities. As a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:52.960
the rebels authorize a raid on Lothal, where&nbsp;
the nuts and bolts of the project are located.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:58.360
The attack is an abject failure, however, with&nbsp;
nearly every rebel pilot killed and their leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:03.800
Hera Syndulla, captured. With his factory safe,&nbsp;
Thrawn is informed of a new threat to his TIE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:08.480
Defender project: Project Stardust,&nbsp;
otherwise known as the Death Star.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.960
"If construction of the Defender is to continue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:14.160
you must make your case directly&nbsp;
to the Emperor himself."

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.120
Concerned about the Empire's dedication&nbsp;
to this hugely expensive project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:22.400
Thrawn decides to meet with Palpatine&nbsp;
personally on Coruscant. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:28.240
Thrawn's journey to meet with Palpatine proves to&nbsp;
be the end of his project, as Governor Pryce blows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:34.320
up all of the fuel for the TIE Defenders in a&nbsp;
successful attempt to kill the Jedi Kanan Jarrus.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.240
The end of the TIE Defender project&nbsp;
holds major implications for the galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.280
as it spurs Palpatine to throw his&nbsp;
support behind Project Stardust. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:49.360
is also a massive blow for Thrawn, as his avenue&nbsp;
of gaining favor with the Emperor is closed off.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:53.240
Following the failure of the TIE Defender&nbsp;
project, Thrawn is ordered by the Emperor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:59.640
to crush the rebellion on Lothal and capture the&nbsp;
young Jedi Ezra Bridger. Thrawn, eager to regain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:04.560
favor with the Emperor to help save his people,&nbsp;
brings the might of the Seventh Fleet to bear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:09.520
threatening to blow up the capital city unless&nbsp;
the Jedi surrenders. After ensuring Ezra is in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.400
the hands of the Emperor, Thrawn returns to&nbsp;
the bridge of his capital ship, the Chimaera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:19.440
and orders the fleet to bombard the planet.&nbsp;
The shelling of the capital does nothing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:24.440
however, as the rebels on the ground manage&nbsp;
to raise a planetary defense shield in time.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:28.000
Although Thrawn sends his bodyguard,&nbsp;
Rukh, to shut down the planetary shield,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:32.320
the rebels manage to fight off the Imperial&nbsp;
forces and ensure the shield's functionality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:37.240
Upon hearing of Rukh's death, Ezra enters the&nbsp;
bridge and demands Thrawn's surrender. Although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:41.800
Thrawn was still planning on continuing the&nbsp;
fight, he is forestalled by the arrival of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:47.120
purrgil — large space whales that are capable of&nbsp;
lightspeed. The purrgil completely decimate the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:51.680
entirety of Thrawn's fleet, with one smashing&nbsp;
into the bridge of the Chimaera and wrapping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:57.400
its tendrils around Thrawn, fulfilling the Bendu's&nbsp;
vision of the Grand Admiral's defeat. The purrgil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:02.640
then jump to lightspeed, flinging both Ezra&nbsp;
and Thrawn to an unknown destination in space&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:07.763
and completely destroying any hope Thrawn&nbsp;
had of using the Empire to save his people.

00:10:07.763 --> 00:10:10.680
"Um… was that the plan?"

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:16.640
In 1991, author Timothy Zahn wrote Heir to the&nbsp;
Empire. This novel, which was later adapted into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:21.760
a comic series, chronicled the adventures&nbsp;
of Luke Skywalker, Leia Organa, Han Solo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:26.640
and their merry band of Rebels following the&nbsp;
events of Return of the Jedi. Set approximately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:31.320
five years later, Grand Admiral Thrawn is&nbsp;
introduced as the next in line to restart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:36.400
the Galactic Empire and crush the New Republic.&nbsp;
The story continues with the novels Dark Force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:41.520
Rising and The Last Command, in which Thrawn's&nbsp;
plans are thwarted by Luke and his allies.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:45.920
A few years later, the author wrote two more&nbsp;
novels to follow up his trilogy; this is known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:51.000
as the Hand of Thrawn duology — and that was&nbsp;
only the beginning. The Grand Admiral would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.840
return to play the role of recurring antagonist&nbsp;
throughout the Extended Universe. For decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:59.720
the original Thrawn trilogy served as the&nbsp;
launching point for the greater Star Wars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:05.880
Expanded Universe, but, when Disney purchased&nbsp;
Lucasfilm in 2012, everything changed. Thrawn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:10.160
like many other characters and stories, was&nbsp;
written out of continuity by the House of Mouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:14.360
with Zahn's acclaimed trilogy being&nbsp;
rebranded under the "Legends" banner.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:19.040
When Thrawn was eventually re-introduced into&nbsp;
the continuity, Lucasfilm made a few significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:24.160
changes to the character. For starters, unlike&nbsp;
in the Heir to the Empire storyline, the Disney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:30.160
versions of Thrawn and Luke never encounter one&nbsp;
another. Instead, Ahsoka Tano and Ezra Bridger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:36.560
serve as Thrawn's main adversaries, with Luke off&nbsp;
elsewhere re-establishing the fallen Jedi Order.

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:42.040
Selling over 15 million copies, Zahn's trilogy&nbsp;
was so successful that his work on Heir to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:46.840
Empire is credited by some with saving the Star&nbsp;
Wars franchise at a time when new adventures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:51.640
were scarce. Following the original theatrical&nbsp;
release of Return of the Jedi and a few other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:56.360
'80s projects that we really don't need to&nbsp;
talk about, Star Wars content had stalled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:00.920
by the early '90s. George Lucas had yet to&nbsp;
develop the prequel trilogy, so Zahn's work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:06.200
single-handedly carried the franchise, opening&nbsp;
the door for more Expanded Universe stories.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:10.400
Though Lucas didn't consider them canon, he&nbsp;
nevertheless took plot beats, characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:14.360
and locations from the EU and added&nbsp;
them to his new films. No doubt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:18.560
Thrawn's popularity among Star Wars fans&nbsp;
was a reason why Zahn's trilogy was so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:23.040
successful. For many years, the Heir to&nbsp;
the Empire trilogy was the closest thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:27.280
to a direct "Star Wars" sequel trilogy&nbsp;
that fans seemed likely to witness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:32.040
as Lucas largely moved on from the franchise&nbsp;
from the mid-'80s to the turn of the century.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:36.640
Thrawn's reappearances in various novels,&nbsp;
games, and comics were quite welcome among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:40.360
fans before Disney swooped in and&nbsp;
took over. It also explains why the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:43.960
character survived the House of Mouse's&nbsp;
purge of the greater Extended Universe;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:48.800
he was too important to fans to be erased&nbsp;
entirely. Perhaps understandably, some fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:53.880
still hold out hope that other characters&nbsp;
from this era could one day return as well.

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:56.280
"No one's ever really gone."

00:12:56.280 --> 00:13:00.480
Grand Admiral Thrawn had the pleasure of&nbsp;
meeting both Anakin Skywalker and Darth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:05.440
Vader during very different phases of the&nbsp;
former Jedi's life. The 2018 novel Thrawn:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:10.760
Alliances revolves around the brief partnership&nbsp;
between the Sith Lord and the warlord as they work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:15.600
together to investigate the Force disturbance&nbsp;
on Batuu. But Alliances doesn't just cover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:19.920
this partnership between Thrawn and Vader&nbsp;
— it also flashes back to the Clone Wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:24.240
when Thrawn and the young Skywalker&nbsp;
worked together to save Padmé Amidala.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:29.680
During this time, Thrawn deduces that Anakin is a&nbsp;
Jedi. Although Anakin believes his role as a Jedi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:34.880
was obvious, given the color of his lightsaber,&nbsp;
Thrawn explains his hesitation. He tells Anakin:

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:38.880
"Our myths of the Republic speak of&nbsp;
two groups of beings with such powers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:43.960
the Jedi, and the Sith. But the Sith are&nbsp;
reputed to be clever and capable warriors."

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:48.880
As it turns out, Anakin's numerous mistakes in&nbsp;
combat allowed Thrawn to correctly identify him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:53.720
as a Jedi. Years later, Emperor Palpatine&nbsp;
tells Thrawn of Skywalker's death following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:59.080
the Clone Wars. Despite this lie, the Chiss&nbsp;
double agent quickly deduces that Lord Vader&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:03.680
and the former General Skywalker are one and&nbsp;
the same. As one of the only people in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:10.080
galaxy to uncover this safeguarded information,&nbsp;
Thrawn keeps it to himself. Smart move, Thrawn.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:14.160
Since the Chiss are so far removed from the&nbsp;
known galaxy, they have little to no knowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:19.200
of society in the Republic. Nevertheless, the&nbsp;
Force still extends into the Unknown Regions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:23.720
even if the people who reside there don't&nbsp;
actually know what it is. For the Chiss people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:27.920
Force-sensitive children may not have&nbsp;
the same giftings as other races do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:32.240
but they still retain a premonition&nbsp;
ability which they call "Third Sight."

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:35.800
Because of their ability to peer into&nbsp;
the future, children with "Third Sight"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:39.880
are conscripted to become space-faring&nbsp;
navigators, since the Chiss don't use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:44.280
traditional technological navigation.&nbsp;
Thrawn's older sister Kivu'rik'ardok,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:48.160
otherwise known as Vurika, was one&nbsp;
of these Force-sensitive children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:53.080
and was taken when Thrawn was just a boy. As an&nbsp;
adult, like many Chiss children with Third Sight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:58.800
Vurika lost her precognitive abilities and instead&nbsp;
worked as an instructor for future navigators.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:03.200
Despite being siblings, when confronted with the&nbsp;
chance to finally meet her long-lost brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:06.080
Vurika, now known as Borika, after her marriage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:11.360
weeps, believing that there is no point since her&nbsp;
memories of Thrawn have long faded. Tragically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:16.080
despite having once believed that one day he&nbsp;
might use his resources to find her, Thrawn never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:22.240
reunites with his sister. Eventually, he comes&nbsp;
to respect her wishes for anonymity and moves on.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:26.960
The events of the Star Wars Rebels finale,&nbsp;
in which Ezra Bridger and Thrawn are thrown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:31.880
into the unknown, are set in the same&nbsp;
year as the original Star Wars film.

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:34.600
"I find your lack of faith disturbing."

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:39.760
In that movie, the Empire loses Grand Moff&nbsp;
Tarkin and the first Death Star at the hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:45.920
of Luke Skywalker and the Rebel Alliance. After&nbsp;
these two enormous defeats, the Emperor tasks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:50.960
Darth Vader with personally overseeing the&nbsp;
destruction of the rebels. In Star Wars #8,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:56.880
which is set after Vader's showdown with Luke on&nbsp;
Cloud City, Palpatine claims that Thrawn or Tarkin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.880 --> 00:16:02.120
would have been perfect for this job and laments&nbsp;
that both are gone. Though the task delays the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:07.720
Sith Lord's search for his long-lost son, Vader&nbsp;
deems it necessary for the health of the Empire.

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:11.400
In Thrawn's absence, Darth Vader&nbsp;
continues to hunt down the rebels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:15.360
During the so-called "War of the Bounty&nbsp;
Hunters," he comes close to capturing Han&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:20.440
Solo and a number of his allies but ultimately&nbsp;
fails. Had Thrawn still been around, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:24.880
these events might not have gone as well for Luke&nbsp;
and his friends, and it's entirely possible that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:29.760
Luke may have been captured prior to his&nbsp;
surrender in Return of the Jedi. Likewise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:35.040
Vader's position overseeing construction of the&nbsp;
second Death Star may have been held by someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:41.120
else had Thrawn or Tarkin survived, meaning his&nbsp;
turn back to the light may never have occurred.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:45.120
Although Thrawn is often seen as a ruthless&nbsp;
leader, willing to do whatever it takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:48.960
for the sake of his ambitions, this&nbsp;
couldn't be further from the truth.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:54.040
From his youth into his Imperial career, Thrawn&nbsp;
always believes that every life holds some sort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:59.320
of value. Though he has no problem eliminating&nbsp;
his enemies, he sees the deaths of innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:05.280
civilians as senseless and unnecessary. In the&nbsp;
novel Thrawn Ascendancy: Greater Good, he says:

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:07.680
"All lives are important, and I resist the thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:11.520
of standing by and watching two&nbsp;
hundred possibly needless deaths."

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:15.400
This was especially true of Thrawn&nbsp;
when he served in the Chiss military,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:18.840
but it generally carries over to&nbsp;
his time with the Empire as well.

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:23.600
Generally speaking, Thrawn also shows deep&nbsp;
respect for his enemies, but this only goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:29.200
so far. In Star Wars Rebels, Thrawn unleashes&nbsp;
his full fury on the Lothal system near the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:34.520
end of his time there. After his increasingly&nbsp;
futile attempts to put the insurgency down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:39.440
he fires on the people of Capital City until&nbsp;
Ezra Bridger surrenders himself to the Empire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:44.280
It's worth noting that these actions come about&nbsp;
due to intense pressure from Emperor Palpatine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:48.720
who hopes to turn Ezra to the Dark Side&nbsp;
— but Thrawn is certainly still the man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:52.760
in charge during the bombardment. Had&nbsp;
Thrawn been given more time, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:58.000
he may have come up with an alternative solution&nbsp;
that didn't threaten the lives of those below.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:02.160
An interesting shade to the Thrawn&nbsp;
character is the Grand Admiral's love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:06.680
or at least appreciation, of traditional&nbsp;
art and music. Believing the arts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:10.160
be a window into the history and&nbsp;
culture of different people groups,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:15.534
Thrawn sees it as a valuable tool to be used&nbsp;
to better understand his allies and opponents.

00:18:15.534 --> 00:18:23.654
"My apologies, Captain Slavin. I forgot that&nbsp;
not everyone is able to appreciate art as I do."

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:29.080
In the Zahn novel Thrawn Ascendancy: Lesser Evil,&nbsp;
a younger Thrawn is shown analyzing hundreds of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:33.240
thousands of different pieces of artwork that&nbsp;
belong to his adoptive family, many of which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:39.160
were created by anonymous artists. He even manages&nbsp;
to connect a series of seemingly unrelated works&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:44.680
together based solely on style and technique,&nbsp;
eventually discovering the artist's identity.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:49.400
Likewise, in Rebels, Thrawn is shown to have&nbsp;
amassed an impressive collection of artwork that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:55.560
all point to the crew of the Ghost, which includes&nbsp;
Ezra Bridger, Sabine Wren, and Hera Syndulla. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:59.960
his time studying their work, he comes to&nbsp;
better understand his enemies and uses this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:05.400
knowledge of their goals and ideals to overpower&nbsp;
them. Across his various media appearances, this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:10.960
appreciation for the arts has remained a strong,&nbsp;
consistent character trait for the Chiss warlord.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:15.320
Though Thrawn isn't much of an artist himself,&nbsp;
his knowledge and understanding of technique&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:20.040
and structure have proven invaluable to his&nbsp;
military campaign. And it's very possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:25.480
that we'll see more of the Grand Admiral's&nbsp;
cultural side in future Star Wars projects.

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:29.840
Though there are any number of military leaders&nbsp;
who could have been the basis for Grand Admiral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:35.920
Thrawn, Zahn revealed the exact source of his&nbsp;
inspiration in a letter written in 2002. He wrote:

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:38.960
"Thrawn isn't based on any one&nbsp;
historical person in particular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:43.960
but is more of a composite of the best and&nbsp;
brightest military geniuses that have ever lived."

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:50.360
On Zahn's list: Hannibal, Alexander the Great,&nbsp;
Robert E. Lee, and Erwin Rommel. Zahn continued to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:56.080
explain Thrawn's characterization by emphasizing&nbsp;
that he, unlike many real-life military leaders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:56.080 --> 00:20:01.000
genuinely cares about those under his command.&nbsp;
The lives of his officers matter to him, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:05.880
he has no desire to see any of them gunned down&nbsp;
for no reason. Since Thrawn was supposed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:11.160
a different sort of villain than Darth Vader, who&nbsp;
ruled his underlings by fear, he was made into "a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:16.360
tactical genius," a man who would be so respected&nbsp;
by his men that they would "follow him anywhere."

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:21.760
But Zahn wasn't only inspired by the historical&nbsp;
leaders of old to create Thrawn; he was also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:26.360
inspired by popular fictional characters —&nbsp;
including a few who wouldn't have been all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:31.360
that fond of the Grand Admiral's allegiances.&nbsp;
For example, Sir Arthur Conan Doyle's famous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:36.520
detective Sherlock Holmes was a clear template&nbsp;
for Thrawn's ability to piece together a mystery.

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:38.920
"Elementary, my dear Watson. Purely elementary."

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:42.560
Of course, although Holmes uses his&nbsp;
exceptional mind to help others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:48.400
Thrawn uses it to advance the goals of the Empire…&nbsp;
which is a little less noble, to say the least.

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:52.480
Despite being the beloved antagonist of&nbsp;
the most well-received Star Wars novels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:56.600
the editors at Marvel Comics reportedly&nbsp;
had no initial interest in including the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:56.600 --> 00:21:00.880
infamous Grand Admiral in their ongoing&nbsp;
Star Wars titles. According to former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:05.000
Marvel assistant editor Heather Antos, who&nbsp;
took to Twitter to show her support for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:10.280
Thrawn's re-introduction into the franchise, a&nbsp;
"very important higher up" at Marvel told her:

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:13.120
"The blue guy? No one cares about him."

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.600
Of course, it was only a few years later&nbsp;
that Thrawn would get his own comic series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:21.720
in support of his debut on Rebels. Clearly,&nbsp;
someone had a change of heart. And ever since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:25.880
his successful return, Thrawn has become a&nbsp;
recurring character throughout the greater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:30.720
Star Wars universe. Be it the different Marvel&nbsp;
comic books, various Thrawn-themed novels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:35.600
or his presence in the live-action shows,&nbsp;
it's clear that Thrawn is here to stay.

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:38.960
And of course, with the announcement&nbsp;
of Dave Filoni's upcoming movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:44.800
which is set to round off the stories begun by The&nbsp;
Mandalorian, The Book of Boba Fett, and Ahsoka,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:51.080
there's also a lot to look forward to as Thrawn&nbsp;
expands his grasp over the Star Wars franchise.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:54.600
In addition to the Thrawn trilogy that&nbsp;
Timothy Zahn penned in the early '90s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:59.440
the author found the chance to tackle the&nbsp;
character on a number of occasions afterward.

00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:04.280
Though Zahn wrote various sequel stories featuring&nbsp;
Thrawn that took place after The Last Command,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:08.400
he also took on a number of novels set&nbsp;
in the Disney continuity. The first of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:12.680
the new Thrawn trilogy was Star Wars:&nbsp;
Thrawn, which was followed up by Thrawn:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:18.000
Alliances and Thrawn: Treason. These projects&nbsp;
allowed the character's creator to reintroduce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:22.440
him to Star Wars as the protagonist of&nbsp;
his own story. And it didn't end there.

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:27.400
Though Zahn had reinvented Thrawn, helping&nbsp;
transition him from "Legends" into canon, he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:33.000
more stories to tell concerning the Grand Admiral.&nbsp;
In 2020, another Thrawn-based novel — titled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:37.760
Thrawn Ascendancy: Chaos Rising — was published by&nbsp;
Zahn, this one exploring the character's history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:37.760 --> 00:22:43.560
with his people, the Chiss, and their rivalry with&nbsp;
the Grysk. Known as the Thrawn Ascendancy trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:50.040
Zahn continued Thrawn's pre-Clone Wars story with&nbsp;
Greater Good in 2021 and Lesser Evil later that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:54.680
year, rounding out his overhaul of the character's&nbsp;
past and forever changing the way fans saw the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:59.200
Chiss legend. Knowing that Zahn is involved&nbsp;
in future Thrawn stories should give Star Wars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:06.000
loyalists hope that, however the Grand Admiral&nbsp;
is adapted next, his creator won't be far behind.

